**Decision: AVOID.** Quality is good (ROIC 21.8%/ROCE 26.3% TTM, rising; Piotroski F 7; regulatory moat from Certificate-of-Need laws) but valuation is unattractive: HCA trades at a premium to its own 5y multiple range (P/E 81st percentile) and well above peers UHS/THC/CYH/ENSG on every multiple (P/E +73%, EV/EBITDA +29%, EV/Sales +61%, P/FCF +31%), while the fact sheet's own-history base-case fair value (396.35 USD) sits 10.9% below the last close (445.01 USD). Net margin has compressed 2.9pp over 5y on payer-mix/exchange-patient headwinds, and leverage (3.20x net debt/EBITDA, rising) and Altman Z (2.64, grey zone) leave limited cushion. Good business, priced for more than the evidence supports — below the conviction bar for a BUY.
