**Decision: AVOID (conviction 3, not investable size).** Cash-flow multiples (P/FCF 5.0x, FCF yield ~20%) look statistically cheap, but five years of consistent gross/operating/net margin compression and an ROE collapse from 17.2% to 3.2% show no durable moat — Reuters-reported share loss to Asian rivals and a weak Q3 (unit sales -5.5%, EV sales down) confirm the trend is still live. The fair-value base case (+91.9%) requires a margin recovery the evidence doesn't yet support; the bear case (-13.4%) is a more faithful read of the current trajectory. Buybacks are being funded into margin deterioration rather than reinvestment. Re-test if gross margin and ROE stabilize per the invalidation triggers in the note.
